refsection.para:
          The C++ methods defined here are the operators that
          modify the object in-place:

ArithmeticOutputVal& a;
ArithmeticOutputVal& b;
a += b;
b *= 123.; 

          Non-member binary operators that return a new
          ArithmeticOutputVal are defined only
          for the concrete derived classes and for the reference
          counted &ArithmeticOutputValue; wrapper.

